        "user_title": "",
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>1. &nbsp;Baron Blade&#39;s episode is my favorite so far. &nbsp;A lot of background and a story that goes from being the main villain to at least becoming a hero in the end. &nbsp;The hero part was temporary but still a neat transition along with the questions from heroes about why he has these Doomsday devices. &nbsp;I&#39;m more curious about his role in the RPG as wwell because of this. &nbsp;It also had one of the&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">biggest reveals to me in that </span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">he founded RevoCorp which up to that point we had no idea on any of their background.&nbsp;</span></p><p>2. &nbsp;The Setback episode is my least favorite. &nbsp;I feel there was a lot of more story to tell of his conflicts with RevoCorp between Plague Rat and Revenant that the questions didn&#39;t get into at all. &nbsp;</p><p>3 &amp; 4. I don&#39;t have a most or least favorite Interlude episode. &nbsp;They&#39;ve all had something to pique my interest.&nbsp;</p>",
